  "note": "Planets with air (scripts/planets.gd, docs/runtime/planets.md). Every system's main world gets a downport on its surface (site kind 'world') near its city, and a rough landing field a few km off ('field'); Sol adds a downport on Mars ('mars'). Worlds come from data/world/worlds.json; cities from settlements.json and secondary_settlements.json, or named here where the canon has only a region. air.density is sea-level density against Earth's; scale_km is how fast it thins with height; breathable lists who can breathe it outside without a suit ('all' for everyone). Gravity is in g. Hops to and from a world are not the same both ways: coming down, the air does the braking (down_dv_kms); going up there is nothing for it but fuel (up_dv_kms, scaled by the square root of the world's gravity). Pay is figured on the climb either way, because a load brought down through the heat is not a cheaper load. Every number here is an assumption to tune.",
